            <ArticleTitle>Coexistence of chronic paroxysmal hemicrania and benign cough headache.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>437-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on the coexistence of both chronic paroxysmal hemicrania and cough headache in a middle-aged woman. Typical chronic paroxysmal hemicrania and cough headache episodes appeared independently and responded to indomethacin. The possible pathophysiological significance of this concurrence of both types of indomethacin-responsive pain is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
